	(text "CONTROL VOLTAGE BUFFERS"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 60.198 30.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3.048 3.048)
				(thickness 0.381)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "1b33ad4b-d120-4ea6-9e0b-4773436e56be")
	)
	(text "---------------------------------------\n- Use film capacitors for all in audio path, <= 5%\n- Use THIN film resistors for all in audio path, <= 0.5%\n- R6 and C3 should physically close to CV input pin 2 of VCAs\n- The NTC thermistor (TH1) has a nominal resistance 47k (@25C)\n---------------------------------------\nCV BUFFER DESIGN:\n- CV LPF cutoff = 1/(R2*C1*2pi) = 1/(2pi*22n*24k) = 301Hz\n- CV range rescaling (gain factor) from 3.3V to 0.5V:\n  A = -R3 / (R1+(R4||TH1)) = -24k / (133k+(38.3k||47k))\n    = -0.151515 = -0.5V / 3.3V\n- The -2.5V reference is to offset the CV while rescaling it.\n  - The raw CV is in range 0-3.3V\n  - Just scaling it to range of 0.5V would give 0 to -0.5V,\n    since configuration is inverting\n  - But we need to move up by 73mV to get -427mV to +73mV.\n  - (-2.5V) / (698k+(133k||38.3k||47k)) = -3.49uA\n    And the fraction reaching the summing node is\n    133k / (133k+(38.3k||47k)) = 0.863.\n    Then, -1*-3.49uA*24k*0.863 = 73mV (-1 since inverting)\n    By superposition, that gets added to the scaled voltage\n    to move it up 73mV, bringing it into the right range.\n---------------------------------------\nTEMPERATURE COMPENSATION\n  - The VCA drifts by 0.33% of the gain per deg. C.\n  - I.e. at -20dB gain, chip warming by 15C gives\n    -20dB * 0.33% * 15C = +0.99dB => now -19.01dB\n  - To compensate CV scaling, need 0.33% * 133k\n    = +439R / degC, make CV smaller, to cancel temp.\n  - This 47k NTC thermistor does 447R per C (close)\n  - Paralleling it with R4 makes it more linear\n    (by default NTC is exponental, R4 helps extremes)\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 300.736 84.328 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.905 1.905)
				(italic yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "1cc9581c-d34e-4311-a770-bf2602427594")
	)
	(text "BOARD CONNECTORS"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 51.816 224.282 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3.048 3.048)
				(thickness 0.381)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "26329650-97b0-4480-9426-d28d908abfd5")
	)
	(text "Logic CV Follower/Buffers"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 160.782 169.926 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
				(thickness 0.381)
				(bold yes)
				(italic yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "379b8b1b-22d0-4d63-94cf-77306ce598ac")
	)
	(text "CV Buffer Functions:\n1. Buffer to drive the VCA CV input\n2. LPF at ~301Hz, Sallen Key two pole\n3. Rescale 3.3V range to 0.5V range\n   (Gives 82dB of gain control range)\n4. Shift range to 73mV to -427mV\n   (73mV = +12dB, -427mV = -70dB)\n5. Correct temperature drift by scaling CV\n   to compensate (using NTC thermistor)\n\n** Neg. Temp. Coeff. (NTC) Thermistor\n   Part No. NTCLE100E3473JB0 Vishay"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 37.338 151.892 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.905 1.905)
				(italic yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "4cf175f4-1981-4e13-a83e-89f69684fa64")
	)
